## Completion evidence
Publication preparation reviews the existing bounded glossary, icon sizing and
invitation-control delivery. Their earlier technical evidence remains scoped
to fictional/offline qualification, not current live LinkedIn acceptance.
The user explicitly selects a project-only public handoff rather than exporting
the original private continuity. Four independently authored public files and
their exact ignore exceptions implement that boundary.

Before edits, independently capture all 36 predecessor issue/item snapshots,
stored mappings and numbered sources, the original private continuity identities
and the unchanged published v0.2.4 release identity.

The exact original-source integration passes all 180 selected invitation/GUI
cases with required fictional-browser mode, zero skips, failures or errors.
Focused Ruff and Black pass for all six modified Python files; mypy passes for
the four modified runtime modules. Context allow/deny checks pass for the four
reviewed public files, original private continuity, social/inbox paths,
unreviewed future context and existing private-input exclusions. The original
private store retains exact bytes and modification times. These checks do not
send invitations or establish live LinkedIn qualification.

Actual commit/push and independent remote verification are still pending.

